{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed218530468/12/prompt.md | sed -n '1,240p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n     2\t\n     3\t每个参考题描述包含：\n     4\t- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n     5\t- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n     6\t- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n     7\t- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n     8\t\n     9\t参考题目如下：\n    10\t<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"8a6d367c\" lines=\"52-67\">\n    11\t<description>\n    12\tComplete the framed area by expanding the unique upper template that contains the existing seed pixels.\n    13\t\n    14\tInput structure:\n    15\t- A teal background contains small colored template masks above a larger rectangular frame.\n    16\t- The frame encloses one fill color arranged as a partial block-scaled copy of one template.\n    17\t- The frame interior dimensions are an integer square scale of the matching template bbox.\n    18\t\n    19\tRule:\n    20\t- Crop to the rectangular frame.\n    21\t- Identify the unique upper template whose block-scaled mask covers every existing fill pixel inside the frame.\n    22\t- Reset the frame interior to background and paint the whole scaled mask with the fill color.\n    23\t\n    24\tKey insight:\n    25\tThe lower colored pixels are seed cells that reveal which upper template should be completed inside the frame.\n    26\t</description>\n    27\t</reference_puzzle>\n    28\t\n    29\t<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"cf5fd0ad\" lines=\"10-22\">\n    30\t<description>\n    31\tBuild a four-quadrant rotational tiling of the input square.\n    32\t\n    33\tInput structure\n    34\t- The input is a square grid treated as one complete sprite.\n    35\t\n    36\tRule\n    37\t- Each output quadrant is a 2x2 repetition of a rotated copy of the whole input.\n    38\t- The quadrant rotations are upper-left 180 degrees, upper-right 90 degrees\n    39\t  clockwise, lower-left 90 degrees counterclockwise, and lower-right unchanged.\n    40\t\n    41\tKey insight\n    42\t- The output is a 4x4 grid of original-size blocks, not a per-pixel scale-up.\n    43\t</description>\n    44\t</reference_puzzle>\n    45\t\n    46\t<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"a6f40cea\" lines=\"74-88\">\n    47\t<description>\n    48\tComplete partial paths inside a framed rectangle by projecting external color traces inward.\n    49\t\n    50\tInput structure:\n    51\t- bg, a 1px rectangular frame (border color) with uniform interior fill.\n    52\t- Colored components outside the frame touching its edges.\n    53\t\n    54\tRule:\n    55\t- Output = the frame's interior, filled with the fill color.\n    56\t- Map each outside component's frame-touch points into interior coordinates.\n    57\t- Monochrome components become solid Manhattan stripes between mapped endpoints.\n    58\t- Two-color components become alternating-color Manhattan paths.\n    59\t\n    60\tKey insight: Endpoint colors of two-color traces anchor the alternating phase deterministically.\n    61\t</description>\n    62\t</reference_puzzle>\n    63\t\n    64\t<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2ccd9fef\" lines=\"173-187\">\n    65\t<description>\n    66\tPredict the next panel in a framed sequence by continuing each scheduled colored interval.\n    67\t\n    68\tInput structure\n    69\t- The grid is made from three or more equal panels in one row or one column.\n    70\t- The final input panel is the static target template; every earlier panel differs from it only by dynamic colors absent from the template.\n    71\t- Each dynamic color appears in a regular temporal schedule across the earlier panels.\n    72\t\n    73\tRule\n    74\t- Keep the final template panel as the output canvas.\n    75\t- For every dynamic color whose schedule reaches the next panel, compare its last two appearances.\n    76\t- Extrapolate each one-dimensional interval along the color's changing row or column axis and paint that predicted mask.\n    77\t\n    78\tKey insight\n    79\t- The task is not asking for the last visible panel, but for the next frame after the blank/template slot.\n    80\t</description>\n    81\t</reference_puzzle>\n    82\t\n    83\t<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"ecb67b6d\" lines=\"138-155\">\n    84\t<description>\n    85\tRecolor the grey diagonal-chain regions in an orange field to teal.\n    86\t\n    87\tInput structure\n    88\tThe input contains only grey pixels and orange pixels.  Grey pixels form\n    89\tseveral 8-connected regions embedded in the orange field.\n    90\t\n    91\tRule\n    92\tDecompose each grey 8-connected region into 4-connected lobes.  Recolor the\n    93\twhole region teal only when it contains a straight diagonal run of at least\n    94\tthree pixels and those lobes meet only by diagonal corner contacts in a\n    95\tnon-branching diagonal chain or cycle; a single 4-connected region is\n    96\trecolored only when it is a square diagonal staircase.\n    97\t\n    98\tKey insight\n    99\tThe teal regions are not selected by size or position; they are the grey\n   100\tregions whose internal connectivity depends on diagonal corner joins, while\n   101\tsame-edge cracks, rectangles, bars, and branching/noisy regions remain grey.\n   102\t</description>\n   103\t</reference_puzzle>\n   104\t\n   105\t<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"48634b99\" lines=\"14-27\">\n   106\t<description>\n   107\tAdvance the marker from one half of a vertical bar to the same half of the next longer bar.\n   108\t\n   109\tInput structure\n   110\t- The grid has one dominant background color and exactly two foreground colors.\n   111\t- One foreground color forms many vertical one-cell-wide bars; the other appears as a single vertical marker segment.\n   112\t- The marker segment occupies exactly the top or bottom half of its containing vertical bar.\n   113\tRule\n   114\t- Recolor the current marker segment back to the bar color.\n   115\t- Find the unique all-bar-color vertical bar whose height is two pixels greater than the marked source bar.\n   116\t- Recolor the same half of that next longer bar to the marker color.\n   117\tKey insight\n   118\t- Each bar's total height encodes an ordered size, and the marker advances from a 2k bar to the corresponding 2(k+1) bar while preserving whether it marks the top or bottom half.\n   119\t</description>\n   120\t</reference_puzzle>\n   121\t\n   122\t<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"fd02da9e\" lines=\"26-41\">\n   123\t<description>\n   124\tReplace each colored corner marker with its corner-specific inward stencil in the same color.\n   125\t\n   126\tInput structure\n   127\t- The grid is 8x8 with a single dominant background color.\n   128\t- Foreground pixels are marker pixels, each located at one of the four corners.\n   129\t- A marker's color is carried to the stencil selected by its corner position.\n   130\t\n   131\tRule\n   132\t- Erase each corner marker back to the background.\n   133\t- Top corner markers become an inward 2x2 block one cell away from the top and side edges.\n   134\t- Bottom corner markers become the mirrored three-pixel inward bent stencil shown by the bottom-corner examples.\n   135\t\n   136\tKey insight\n   137\t- The marker position selects the fixed stencil; the marker color only supplies the paint color, so multiple corners apply independently.\n   138\t</description>\n   139\t</reference_puzzle>\n   140\t\n   141\t<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"dd6b8c4b\" lines=\"9-22\">\n   142\t<description>\n   143\tMove the closest reachable maroon pixels into the 3×3 block around the unique red center.\n   144\t\n   145\tInput structure:\n   146\t- bg = orange floor, magenta walls, scattered maroon (9) pixels.\n   147\t- A unique red (2) pixel marks the center of a 3×3 destination block.\n   148\t\n   149\tRule:\n   150\t- Maroon pixels connected to the destination through floor/maroon cells (not blocked by walls) are candidates.\n   151\t- Rank candidates by distance to the destination; the closest ones fill the block in row-major order.\n   152\t- Moved maroons are erased (replaced with floor color).\n   153\t\n   154\tKey insight: Wall barriers restrict connectivity — only maroon pixels reachable via flood-fill through the floor qualify, so proximity alone isn't enough.\n   155\t</description>\n   156\t</reference_puzzle>\n   157\t\n   158\t<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"4a1cacc2\" lines=\"8-23\">\n   159\t<description>\n   160\tFill the rectangle from the lone foreground pixel to its nearest grid corner.\n   161\t\n   162\tInput structure\n   163\t- The grid is a uniform background field with exactly one foreground pixel.\n   164\t- The foreground pixel's color is the color used for all added pixels.\n   165\t\n   166\tRule\n   167\t- Find the grid corner with the smallest Manhattan distance to the foreground pixel.\n   168\t- Recolor every pixel in the inclusive axis-aligned rectangle bounded by that\n   169\t  corner and the foreground pixel to the foreground color.\n   170\t\n   171\tKey insight\n   172\t- The single pixel is one corner of the rectangle; the opposite corner is the\n   173\t  nearest corner of the whole canvas.\n   174\t</description>\n   175\t</reference_puzzle>\n   176\t\n   177\t<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9f669b64\" lines=\"26-48\">\n   178\t<description>\n   179\tPush the central solid rectangle to the grid edge, splitting the perpendicular target rectangle around its path.\n   180\t\n   181\tInput structure\n   182\t- The background is the dominant color.\n   183\t- There are exactly three monochrome foreground objects arranged on one\n   184\t  horizontal or vertical axis.\n   185\t- The middle object on that axis is a solid rectangular moving object.\n   186\t- One end object is a solid rectangle or bar whose long side is perpendicular\n   187\t  to the movement axis; this is the target to split.\n   188\t\n   189\tRule\n   190\t- Move the middle rectangle along the axis toward the target until it is\n   191\t  flush with the grid edge in that direction.\n   192\t- Clear the original middle rectangle and the original target.\n   193\t- Split the target through the moving rectangle's two-cell-wide path and\n   194\t  shift the two halves one cell outward perpendicular to the movement.\n   195\t- Keep the other end object unchanged.\n   196\t\n   197\tKey insight\n   198\t- The non-target end object acts as a pusher; the central rectangle travels\n   199\t  away from it through the perpendicular target, opening a matching gap.\n   200\t</description>\n   201\t</reference_puzzle>\n   202\t\n   203\t<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"ac6f9922\" lines=\"18-40\">\n   204\t<description>\n   205\tSummarize the enclosed table slots by the single object color inside each slot, using the slot background color for empty slots.\n   206\t\n   207\tInput structure\n   208\t- The most common color forms the outer background and all enclosed slot\n   209\t  backgrounds.\n   210\t- The enclosed background components form a complete rectangular array of\n   211\t  slots, ordered by their positions.\n   212\t- Each slot contains either no other color or exactly one object color.\n   213\t\n   214\tRule\n   215\t- Find all 4-connected components of the most common color that do not touch\n   216\t  the input edge.\n   217\t- Sort their bounding boxes into row and column order to define the output\n   218\t  table.\n   219\t- For each slot, output its unique non-background color if present; otherwise\n   220\t  output the background color.\n   221\t\n   222\tKey insight\n   223\t- The large grid is an expanded table: the enclosed background components are\n   224\t  the cells, and any colored object drawn inside a cell is that cell's summary\n   225\t  value.\n   226\t</description>\n   227\t</reference_puzzle>\n   228\t\n   229\t<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"4c7dc4dd\" lines=\"7-21\">\n   230\t<description>\n   231\tLearn a transformation rule from a training pair of framed sprites, then apply it to a test sprite.\n   232\t\n   233\tInput structure:\n   234\t- Grid contains several colored square frames (hollow borders of a single color).\n   235\t- Each frame's interior holds a small pattern sprite; one frame's interior is blank (all black).\n   236\t- Two frames form a training pair (their interiors share the same color palette); one remaining frame is the test case.\n   237\t\n   238\tRule:\n   239\t- Identify the training pair by matching interior color sets; the other non-blank frame is the test input.\n   240\t- Infer the rule mapping source→destination (e.g. reflection, color inversion, gap filling, endpoint extraction, or checkerboard complement).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed218530468/12/des.md | sed -n '1,240p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed218530468/12/des.md | sed -n '1,240p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t<new_puzzle>\n     2\t- `description`：将网格中散落的彩色 L 形片段按颜色配对，然后根据灰色目标框角落处的彩色标记确定拼合定位，将每对 L 形拼合成完整的 2x2 方块填入对应目标框内。\n     3\t\n     4\t- `Input structure`：\n     5\t  - 背景为 black。\n     6\t  - 网格中散布着偶数个彩色 L 形对象，每种颜色恰好出现两个 L 形。\n     7\t  - 每个 L 形由 3 个像素组成：两个像素构成一条短边，第三个像素在短边端点处拐弯形成直角。L 形共有四种朝向（开口分别朝左上、右上、左下、右下），同色两个 L 形朝向互补（即它们可以拼合成 2x2 方块）。\n     8\t  - 网格中还有若干个由 grey 像素绘制的空心矩形框（外框 4x4，内部 2x2），数量等于颜色种类数。\n     9\t  - 每个 grey 框的四个外角中恰好有一个角的外侧对角位置上放置了一个单像素彩色标记，颜色对应某一对 L 形的颜色。标记所在的角位置用于指示拼合定位。\n    10\t\n    11\t- `Rule`：\n    12\t  - 第一层推理：通过角落彩色标记的颜色，将 grey 框与同色 L 形对配对。\n    13\t  - 第二层推理：确定拼合方式。彩色标记位于 grey 框的某个角（左上/右上/左下/右下）。在两个同色 L 形中，开口朝向与标记所在角相同的那个 L 形被放置在 2x2 内部的该角对角位置（即标记在左上角，则该 L 形放在 2x2 的右下区域）；另一个 L 形填充剩余像素。\n    14\t  - 输出时，将拼合后的 2x2 彩色实心方块填入对应 grey 框的内部。移除网格中原始散落的 L 形（变为 black）。保留 grey 框和角落标记。\n    15\t\n    16\t- `Key insight`：所有 L 形在视觉上相似，解题者必须先按颜色配对，再通过 grey 框角落标记的位置推断拼合方式。标记点同时编码了颜色匹配和空间定位两层信息，而 L 形朝向与标记角位置之间的\"对角放置\"映射是核心的非显然规律。\n    17\t</new_puzzle>\n    18\t\n    19\t<new_puzzle>\n    20\t- `description`：网格被灰色水平线分为上下两个面板，上面板中的双色交替条带定义编织节奏，下面板中经线与纬线的交叉点根据该节奏决定哪根线显示在上方。\n    21\t\n    22\t- `Input structure`：\n    23\t  - 网格由一条水平的 grey 分隔线分成上下两个面板。\n    24\t  - 上面板（规则面板）：背景为 black，包含若干条水平短色带，每条色带占一行。每条色带由两种颜色交替排列的像素组成（例如 red-blue-red-blue...），不同色带的起始颜色和周期可能不同。每条色带的最左端紧邻一个 yellow 标记像素（位于色带左侧一格）。\n    25\t  - 下面板（编织面板）：背景为 black，包含若干条单像素宽的水平线（纬线）和竖直线（经线），每根线为单一颜色，不同线颜色不同。经线和纬线在若干位置交叉。在输入中，所有交叉点的像素显示为纬线颜色（纬线默认在上）。\n    26\t  - 每根纬线的颜色恰好是上面板中某条色带的两种交替颜色之一。\n    27\t\n    28\t- `Rule`：\n    29\t  - 第一层推理：对每根纬线，在上面板中找到包含该纬线颜色的色带（该纬线颜色是色带两种交替色之一）。\n    30\t  - 第二层推理：读取该色带的交替颜色序列。从左到右沿纬线遍历它与经线的每个交叉点，按顺序对应色带序列中的每个位置。若序列当前位置的颜色等于纬线自身颜色，则该交叉点保持纬线颜色（纬线在上）；若序列当前位置是色带的另一种颜色，则将该交叉点改为经线颜色（经线在上）。\n    31\t  - 非交叉点处的像素不变。上面板保持不变。\n    32\t\n    33\t- `Key insight`：上面板的色带不是装饰，而是编织穿越模式的查找表。每条色带的双色交替节奏编码了对应纬线在交叉点处\"上穿/下穿\"的规律。解题者需要先识别上下面板之间的颜色关联（纬线颜色对应哪条色带），再理解交替序列如何决定交叉点的遮挡关系。\n    34\t</new_puzzle>\n    35\t\n    36\t<new_puzzle>\n    37\t- `description`：网格中若干同色灰色矩形存在空间嵌套关系，根据底部图例条中的颜色序列将各层级矩形的边框着色，并将实心矩形转为空心。\n    38\t\n    39\t- `Input structure`：\n    40\t  - 背景为 black。\n    41\t  - 网格中有若干个 grey 实心矩形（大小各异）。这些矩形之间可能存在嵌套关系：一个矩形完全位于另一个矩形内部（两者之间有至少一像素的 black 间隔）。嵌套可达多层（例如大矩形内含中矩形，中矩形内含小矩形）。同一层级内可有多个并列矩形。\n    42\t  - 网格最底部一行是一条\"图例条\"：由若干种不同颜色的像素从左到右依次排列（每种颜色占一个像素，颜色之间无间隔），颜色数量等于最大嵌套层级数。图例条中从左到右第 1 个颜色对应最外层（第 1 层），第 2 个颜色对应第 2 层，依此类推。\n    43\t\n    44\t- `Rule`：\n    45\t  - 第一层推理：识别所有 grey 矩形并分析其空间包含关系，确定嵌套层级。不被任何矩形包含的为第 1 层，被恰好一个矩形包含的为第 2 层，被两层矩形包含的为第 3 层，依此类推。\n    46\t  - 第二层推理：读取图例条中的颜色序列，建立层级到颜色的映射：第 k 层对应图例条从左数第 k 个颜色。\n    47\t  - 第三层推理：将每个 grey 实心矩形转换为空心矩形——仅保留最外围一像素宽的边框，边框颜色使用该矩形层级对应的图例颜色；矩形内部变为 black（除了被更内层矩形覆盖的区域）。\n    48\t  - 输出中图例条被移除（该行变为 black）。\n    49\t\n    50\t- `Key insight`：所有矩形在输入中都是同一种 grey 色，解题者无法靠颜色区分层级，必须通过空间包含关系推断嵌套深度。图例条提供层级到颜色的映射，但映射的\"键\"需要从几何嵌套中自行推导。这使得问题具有三层结构：识别嵌套、读取图例、执行变换。\n    51\t</new_puzzle>\n    52\t\n    53\t<new_puzzle>\n    54\t- `description`：网格中彩色种子像素长在灰色树形路径的叶端外侧，每个种子沿远离树的方向生长出一条同色线段，线段长度等于该叶端到最近分叉点的路径距离。\n    55\t\n    56\t- `Input structure`：\n    57\t  - 背景为 black。\n    58\t  - grey 像素构成若干条互相连接的单像素宽直线段（仅水平或竖直），这些线段形成树形结构（无环路）。线段交汇处为分叉点——该位置的 grey 像素有 3 个或 4 个与其正交相邻的 grey 像素。\n    59\t  - 树的末端为叶节点——该位置的 grey 像素仅有 1 个正交相邻的 grey 像素。\n    60\t  - 每个叶节点向外延伸的方向上（即叶节点远离其唯一 grey 邻居的那一侧），紧邻放置一个非 grey、非 black 的彩色像素（种子）。种子不在 grey 路径上。\n    61\t  - 不同种子颜色可能相同也可能不同。\n    62\t\n    63\t- `Rule`：\n    64\t  - 第一步：对每个种子，找到它紧邻的叶节点。从叶节点出发沿 grey 路径向内行走（每次移动到下一个正交相邻的 grey 像素），直到到达第一个分叉点（有 3 个或更多正交 grey 邻居的节点）或到达另一个叶节点（路径上没有分叉点的情况）。记录行走的步数 D。\n    65\t  - 第二步：从种子像素的位置出发，沿种子远离叶节点的方向（即从叶节点到种子的方向继续延伸），绘制同色像素共 D 个（不含种子本身，即在种子外侧再画 D-1 个同色像素加上种子自身共 D 个像素；若种子已占一格则额外画 D-1 格）。如果到达网格边界则提前停止。\n    66\t  - grey 路径结构在输出中保持不变。\n    67\t\n    68\t- `Key insight`：种子生长长度不是固定的，而是由树形路径的局部拓扑结构——从叶端到最近分叉点的分支长度——决定的。解题者需要在 grey 网络中识别分叉点，为每个种子沿路径丈量分支长度，然后按该长度向外延伸。路径的几何结构直接编码了生长参数。\n    69\t</new_puzzle>\n    70\t\n    71\t<new_puzzle>\n    72\t- `description`：网格中若干彩色对象各自携带一个方向标记像素，对象需要被旋转后填入形状匹配的灰色轮廓框中，旋转角度由对象标记方向到轮廓标记方向的差异决定。\n    73\t\n    74\t- `Input structure`：\n    75\t  - 背景为 black。\n    76\t  - 网格中散布若干个小型彩色对象（每个对象为一个四连通区域，占据约 3x3 到 5x5 的范围）。每个对象由一种\"主体色\"（非 yellow、非 black、非 grey）和一个 yellow 像素组成。yellow 像素位于对象边界框的上/下/左/右某一侧的中间位置，作为方向标记。\n    77\t  - 网格中另有若干个由 grey 像素绘制的空心轮廓（单像素宽边框构成的封闭形状）。每个轮廓的内部空间形状与某个对象（经适当旋转后）的主体形状完全吻合。轮廓数量与对象数量相同。\n    78\t  - 每个轮廓的边框上恰好有一个像素被替换为 yellow（位于轮廓边框上/下/左/右某一侧的中间位置），作为轮廓的方向标记。\n    79\t\n    80\t- `Rule`：\n    81\t  - 第一层推理（确定旋转量）：对象的 yellow 标记指示\"当前方向\"，轮廓的 yellow 标记指示\"目标方向\"。计算从当前方向到目标方向需要顺时针旋转的角度（0°/90°/180°/270°），将整个对象（包含主体色像素，不含 yellow 标记）按该角度顺时针旋转。\n    82\t  - 第二层推理（形状匹配配对）：将旋转后的对象主体形状（仅主体色像素）与每个轮廓的内部空间形状比对，找到完全吻合的唯一轮廓。\n    83\t  - 将旋转后的主体色像素填入匹配轮廓的内部。清除对象原始位置的所有像素（变为 black）。保留 grey 轮廓边框和轮廓上的 yellow 标记。\n    84\t\n    85\t- `Key insight`：yellow 标记同时承担两个功能：指示旋转量和辅助形状配对。解题者必须先理解两个标记之间的方向差编码了旋转角度，再利用旋转后的形状匹配来确认配对关系。方向推理与形状匹配互为验证，缺一不可。\n    86\t</new_puzzle>\n    87\t\n    88\t<new_puzzle>\n    89\t- `description`：网格中多对同色像素按连线方向自然分为四组（水平/竖直/两种对角线），仅对像素对数量最多的那一组绘制连接线段，其余组保持端点不变。\n    90\t\n    91\t- `Input structure`：\n    92\t  - 背景为 black。\n    93\t  - 网格中散布若干成对出现的彩色像素。每种非 black 颜色恰好出现 2 个像素，构成一对。不同对颜色各不相同。\n    94\t  - 每对同色像素的相对位置严格属于以下四种方向之一：水平（同行不同列）、竖直（同列不同行）、主对角线方向（行差等于列差，即向右下或左上）、副对角线方向（行差等于列差的相反数，即向右上或左下）。\n    95\t  - 每种方向上至少分布一对像素，且四种方向中有唯一一种包含最多的像素对数量。\n    96\t\n    97\t- `Rule`：\n    98\t  - 第一层推理（方向分类）：对每对同色像素，根据两点相对位置判断其连线方向，将所有像素对归入水平、竖直、主对角线、副对角线四个组。\n    99\t  - 第二层推理（计数投票）：统计每组中像素对的数量，找到数量唯一最多的那一组。\n   100\t  - 第三层推理（选择性连线）：对数量最多组中的每一对像素，沿两端点之间的直线方向绘制连线——将两端点之间所有中间像素填充为该对的颜色。对其余三组的像素对不做任何改变，仅保留原有的两个端点像素。\n   101\t\n   102\t- `Key insight`：解题者需要先发现\"方向\"是隐含的分类维度——外观上不同颜色的像素对被按几何方向归类。然后需要发现仅对数量最大的方向组执行连线操作。方向分类与多数投票是两层独立的非显然推理，表面上看只是散点，规则隐藏在方向统计中。\n   103\t</new_puzzle>\n   104\t\n   105\t<new_puzzle>\n   106\t- `description`：网格中包含一组彩色方块和一个灰色参考图案，每个方块需要按照其颜色在参考图案中出现的行号来确定竖直偏移量，然后整体向下平移该距离。\n   107\t\n   108\t- `Input structure`：\n   109\t  - 背景为 black。\n   110\t  - 网格左侧有一个竖直排列的\"参考列\"：该列中从上到下排列着若干种不同颜色的单像素，每种颜色占一行，颜色之间可能有 black 间隔行。参考列位于网格第 0 列（最左列）。\n   111\t  - 网格右侧区域散布着若干个小型彩色对象（每个对象是一个四连通的同色连通区域，形状各异）。每个对象的颜色一定在参考列中出现过。可能有多个对象颜色相同。\n   112\t\n   113\t- `Rule`：\n   114\t  - 第一层推理：读取参考列，记录每种颜色在参考列中的位置（从上往下数，第一个非 black 像素为位置 1，第二个非 black 像素为位置 2，依此类推）。\n   115\t  - 第二层推理：对每个彩色对象，在参考列中找到与其颜色匹配的位置编号 P。将该对象整体向下平移 P 个像素。若平移后超出网格底部边界则不绘制超出部分。\n   116\t  - 输出中参考列被移除（变为 black）。原始对象位置被清除（变为 black），仅显示平移后的对象。\n   117\t\n   118\t- `Key insight`：参考列看似仅仅是颜色列表，实际上它通过颜色的排列顺序编码了每种颜色对应的位移量。解题者需要先发现参考列中颜色位置与平移距离的对应关系，这是核心的非显然规律。同色对象共享同一位移量，进一步验证了规则的一致性。\n   119\t</new_puzzle>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
